<%#
  Printable faction card sheets. Chrome, colours and the trademark footer come from the public_page
  layout, shared with the privacy and account-deletion pages; only the sheet list below is this
  page's own. The rows come straight from the files FactionCardPdf wrote into public/cards/pdf.
%>
<% content_for :title, "Printable Cards" %>
<% content_for :footer_extra do %>
  See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
<% end %>
<% content_for :styles do %>
  .sheets { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .sheets li { margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .sheet {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .9rem;
    padding: .85rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .sheet:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .sheet .name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .sheet .detail { color: var(--subtle); font-size: .85rem; }
  .sheet .grow { flex: 1; }
  .sheet .action { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: .9rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .swatch { width: 10px; height: 34px; border-radius: 3px; flex: none; }
  .empty {
    padding: 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: var(--subtle);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .sheet { flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .sheet .grow { flex-basis: 100%; }
  }
<% end %>

<h1>Printable Cards</h1>
<p class="meta">Carnevale Companion &middot; one PDF per faction, ready to print and cut</p>

<p>
  Every model in a faction, as a print-ready PDF. Each page holds one card &mdash; its front and
  back side by side &mdash; at the exact tarot size of <strong>70 &times; 120&nbsp;mm</strong>, with
  thin crop marks to cut against. Cards run in the same order as the app: Leaders first, then
  Heroes, then Henchmen, alphabetical within each.
</p>

<% if @sheets.any? %>
  <ul class="sheets">
    <% @sheets.each do |sheet| %>
      <li>
        <a class="sheet" href="<%= sheet.url %>" download>
          <span class="swatch" style="<%= faction_swatch_style(sheet.faction) %>"></span>
          <span>
            <span class="name"><%= sheet.faction.capitalize %></span><br>
            <span class="detail">
              Cards as of <%= sheet.date.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>
              &middot; <%= number_to_human_size(sheet.byte_size) %>
            </span>
          </span>
          <span class="grow"></span>
          <span class="action">Download PDF &darr;</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
<% else %>
  <p class="empty">
    The print sheets have not been generated yet. Please check back shortly.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>Printing them</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Print at <strong>100% / actual size</strong>. Any &ldquo;fit to page&rdquo; or
    &ldquo;shrink oversized pages&rdquo; option will scale the cards off tarot size &mdash; turn it off.</li>
  <li>Use A4 paper. Card stock of around 250&ndash;300&nbsp;g/m&sup2; holds up far better in play than
    ordinary paper.</li>
  <li>Cut along the crop marks: the four short lines around each card meet at its corners.</li>
  <li>The front and back of a card sit next to each other on the same page, so nothing needs to be
    printed double-sided &mdash; cut both out and glue or sleeve them back to back.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Keeping up to date</h2>
<p>
  The date in each file name is the day those cards were generated. Corrections happen, so if you
  printed a card a while ago it is worth comparing against the current sheet &mdash; or against the
  card in the app, which always shows the latest version.
</p>
